// The contract for the call comparison: a caller asks the owner to do something and waits
// for the value back. That is the whole of it, and it is the shape a connect point's
// returning slot has: what `synqt` lowers `slot lookup(int id) -> Row` to.
//
// Two slots rather than one, matching nextjs/app/actions.js, because one number would not
// separate the pipeline from the work. `echo` has an empty body, so what it measures is the
// round trip and the object protocol around it. `lookup` reads a row out of the same seeded
// table the HTTP table's `/db` route reads.
//
// Both return, and that matters: a fire-and-forget slot has no reply to wait for and would
// measure how fast a caller can write to a socket. A QtRemoteObjects slot with a return type
// answers on the replica through a QRemoteObjectPendingReply, which is the round trip.
class CallFeed
{
    SLOT(QByteArray echo(QByteArray payload))
    SLOT(int lookup(int id))
}
